<title>UK: UK Treasury cuts spending control totals for 97,98.</title>
<headline>UK Treasury cuts spending control totals for 97,98.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK Treasury said in its &quot;Red Book&quot; financial statement and budget report it was cutting the government's spending control totals for the next two years.</p>
<p>The control total would be cut by 1.7 billion stg to 266.5 billion for fiscal 1997/8 and by 1.9 billion stg to 273.7 billion for fiscal 1998/9, it said.</p>
<p>The Treasury set a spending control total of 280.9 billion stg for fiscal 1999/2000.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
